# A batch with one change: create a table, as compaction writes it, with a
# vector size and a field list. An ordinary commit writes size 0 and no
# fields, as in batch-several.hex.
# It stands alone, to show the encoding, so its change needn't fit any state. Its
# sequence number, 258, shows a u64's byte order.
# See beta/FORMAT.md. Every fixture uses the database ID 0123456789abcdef fedcba9876543210.

48 43 52 42                                       # batch: magic number "HCRB"
01 00 00 00 00 00 00 00                           # generation: 1
3f 00 00 00 00 00 00 00                           # length: 63 bytes
02 01 00 00 00 00 00 00                           # sequence number: 258
54                                                # T: create a table
04 00                                             # table name: 4 bytes
64 6f 63 73                                       # docs
80 01 00 00                                       # vector size: 384
03 00                                             # fields: 3
05 00                                             # field name: 5 bytes
74 69 74 6c 65                                    # title
03 00                                             # field name: 3 bytes
76 65 63                                          # vec
04 00                                             # field name: 4 bytes
74 61 67 73                                       # tags
7f 5d 71 aa                                       # checksum: 0xaa715d7f, the CRC32C of the 59 bytes before it
